# NOTHING under data/ is version-controlled.
#
# This is routine run output: meshes, channel data, snapshot dumps, GUI run records. It is
# regenerable, there is going to be a lot of it, and none of it is evidence. A single solve
# writes ~42 MB of channel data and a snapshot run 476-966 MB, which is over GitHub's hard
# 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# The evidence for the R&D challenge lives in presentation/ and is tracked there. That
# separation is the mechanism - it replaced an allowlist of individual files, because a
# directory boundary cannot be defeated by a new filename that happens to match a pattern.
#
# data/raw/ holds the research team's k-Wave workspaces: 423 MB, read-only for us, and
# re-obtainable from them.
*
!.gitignore
